# HQ projects page (2026-11-16)
T.update({235: "HQ projects", 236: "Giga, mega and consortium projects led by World Making Members, GCSME and the strategic consortium.", 237: "Projects led directly by World Making Members, GCSME and the strategic consortium. We sort them into four tiers by size and publish only projects the headquarters has approved.", 238: "See the projects", 239: "Propose or take part", 240: "Three bodies lead the projects", 241: "A Korean company, a UK-headquartered network and a consortium formed for each project share the work of planning and delivery.", 242: "World Making Members (WMM)", 243: "A management consulting company founded in Seoul in December 2021. It runs GOV RADAR and, as GCSME's operating company in Korea, handles overseas expansion and project partnerships for Korean firms.", 244: "Runs GOV RADAR", 245: "Overseas expansion and project partnerships", 246: "GCSME's operating company in Korea", 247: "See the introduction →", 248: "Global &amp; Commonwealth SME Club. An international SME network headquartered in London, it has consulted in more than 80 countries within a 193-country network.", 249: "Headquartered in London, UK", 250: "193-country network", 251: "Consulting in 80+ countries", 252: "Strategic consortium", 253: "An online alliance in which universities, research institutes, banks, international organisations, government bodies, embassies, companies and experts form a team for each project.", 254: "A team for each project", 255: "Review by partner-university PhDs", 256: "Online collaboration", 257: "Ask to take part →", 258: "Project tiers", 259: "Four tiers, by total project cost and how the work is shared.", 260: "Gigaproject", 261: "Total cost of US$10 billion or more", 262: "Work such as national infrastructure, new cities and energy, where several countries and institutions move together for more than a decade.", 263: "Megaproject", 264: "Total cost of US$1 billion or more", 265: "Large projects such as industrial parks, power plants and transport networks, with governments and international finance taking part.", 266: "Strategic consortium project", 267: "Delivered by a consortium, whatever the size", 268: "Several organisations split the roles and bid, propose and deliver together.", 269: "Project", 270: "Delivered by the headquarters", 271: "Planned and run directly by World Making Members or GCSME.", 272: "The giga and mega thresholds follow Oxford professor Bent Flyvbjerg's classification of large projects (US$1bn+ mega, US$10bn+ giga).", 273: "Project list", 274: "Only projects approved by the headquarters appear here. Filter by tier and by lead.", 275: "All tiers", 276: "All leads", 277: "World Making Members", 278: "Live", 279: "A platform that shows the agendas, programmes, tenders and risks of 193 UN member states and 23 autonomous and special regions on one screen.", 280: "Learn more →", 281: "Coming soon", 282: "Projects appear here once the headquarters approves them. Tell us your field of interest and we will let you know first when one opens.", 283: "Want to propose or join a project?", 284: "Send your proposal or interest by email. The headquarters will review it and reply. The headquarters never charges membership or training fees for taking part.", 285: "Send an email", 286: "Photos: Raymond Yeung · Parim Sinani · Unsplash · © 2026 GOV RADAR"})

# About page history (2026-11-17)
T.update({287: 'GOV RADAR history', 288: 'Global government programme network expanded', 289: 'Country-by-country research on government policy, budgeted programmes and overseas business opportunities was extended to all 193 UN member states.', 290: 'International tender and programme search launched', 291: 'A tender and deadline board went live for browsing national government programmes and international procurement notices by deadline, sector, contracting authority and original source.', 292: 'World risk information expanded', 293: 'The world situation board and related pages were extended so that war and conflict, natural disasters, epidemics, cyber attacks and other international risks can be checked by country.', 294: 'Preparedness centre built', 295: 'Step-by-step guides and calculators for 30 days, 60 days, 90 days and 1 year help individuals, households and organisations prepare drinking water, food, backup power, communications and evacuation plans.', 296: 'Information reliability principles set', 297: 'Four data principles were published: official sources such as governments and international organisations first, cross-checking of key facts, labelling uncertainty, and keeping a correction record.', 298: 'GOV RADAR project started', 299: 'Work began on a global radar that links the policy direction and public programmes of governments worldwide with Korean companies’ overseas expansion and international business opportunities.', 300: 'Operating company WMM founded', 301: 'WORLD MAKING MEMBERS Co., Ltd. is presented as the operating base of GOV RADAR. The founding month will be confirmed after a final check of the corporate register.'})
